---
title: Assistant
description: Ask questions about your organization instead of clicking around.
---

The assistant is the first thing you see in nullish. There's no dashboard full of charts: if you want to know something, ask.

- "Which invoices are still open?"
- "What's left on the bank account?"
- "How much VAT do we owe for this year?"

Your conversations are kept under **History**, and **New** starts a fresh one.

## Read only or read and edit

By default the assistant is **Read only**: it looks things up but changes nothing. Click the label to switch to **Read and edit** when you want it to create or update things for you, and click again to set it back.

{% aside %}
The assistant can never do more than you can. If your role is reviewer, it stays read only.
{% /aside %}

## Connect your own AI agent

Prefer your own AI, like Claude or ChatGPT? Connect it to nullish over MCP and do your bookkeeping from there.

{% steps %}

1. Open the menu with your name and go to **API keys**, then choose **Create API key**.

2. Give it a **Name**, pick an **Expiration**, and choose **MCP server** as the **Resource**.

3. Pick the **Access**: **Read** to let your agent look things up, **Read and write** to let it create and update things too.

4. Copy the key. It isn't shown again.

5. In your AI agent, add nullish as an MCP server with this key. The [MCP page](/en/developers/mcp/) shows how.

{% /steps %}

Your agent works with your own access, across all your organizations, and the same limits apply as in the app. Delete the key and it loses access immediately.
